The semicolon (;) is used to separate commands in Lyntin.

ex:

	say hello;wave

will send "say hello" and then "wave" to the mud.


If you want to send a ; to the mud (i.e. you don't want it interpreted
as a command separator), do a \ in front of it.

ex:

	say you're super \;)

will send "say you're super ;)" to the mud.

category: manual
